\chapter{Numerics, forecasting, and data-search kernels}
\label{ch:105}
\index{Numerics, forecasting, and data-search kernels}

The numerical inventory has families for scalar operations, data preparation, search, and forecasting. Do not infer callable On1x support for an entire family from one reviewed adapter. The pricing example uses documented source profiles for selected historical-price and optimization calls. More general numerical APIs can carry arrays, mutable state, optional errors and shape constraints that need separate transfer and validation rules.

\section{Verify a deterministic data path}
Construct a tiny ordered history with an expected summary and a case that reaches an out-of-domain status. Run it through the exact reviewed fixture path. Check representation and error treatment at each boundary before using a larger data set. When comparing a prediction algorithm, keep time order, units, missing values and rounding explicit. For a data-search kernel, compare exact expected matches including duplicates and boundary positions. Measure generalization or performance separately from the correctness of the C11 ABI adapter.

